{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work","id":1163401,"title":"Does Moonlit Huntress work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-28T17:12:13-08:00","id":1163401,"title":"Does Moonlit Huntress work?","content":"<i>Arms of the Chosen</i> has inspired me to look back at a number of older Artifacts that I'd like to get the same treatment. One of the things that intrigued me about the paragraph on moonsilver potentials was &quot;cyclic change&quot;, which reminded me of Moonlit Huntress, in the 3rd Edition corebook.<br /> <br /> But after really looking at the attunement bonus, I have misgivings.<br /> <br /> <br /> The bow gives you a +1 non-Charm success to Stealth rolls when you're suffering Initiative Crash. That's a neat idea. Kind of useless if there's no cover to use for an attempt at establishing concealment, though. But at least it makes some sense that if your opponent crashes you (or if you're trying and failing so hard to Disengage that you Crash yourself), you might want to enter stealth and hide for the three turns necessary for your Initiative to reset to base.<br /> <br /> Though it would seem much easier just to shoot your opponent with a withering attack. So you might be able to score an Initiative Shift.<br /> <br /> (Incidentally, <i>where </i>is the rule that tells us attacking from concealment reveals you? I can find that rule alluded in Observer-Deceiving Attack, but it's never actually stated <i>anywhere </i>in the rules on Stealth. I have taken the matter to the Ask The Devs thread.)<br /> <br /> Anyway, taking the Thrown Charm as gospel, Moonlit Hunter forces you to choose between hiding for three rounds -- possibly in the same range band as the person you were struggling to Disengage from -- during which you cannot simply attack to regain Initiative, because the bow offers no way to attack while remaining concealed. And this is assuming that you had any cover in which to conceal yourself, possibly while at close range with a Melee-focused enemy.<br /> <br /> Oh, and remember that you can't flurry an action to hide (again) with anything else, such as the attack action that revealed you. Not without magic that this bow doesn't provide.<br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming you had cover and managed to hide for three turns, you reset to base Initiative. At which point the bow gives you +1 non-Charm success to Disengage actions.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think that if you haven't managed to use your concealment to Disengage already, or got lucky enough to have your enemy leave the range band to look for you elsewhere, you're going to be hurting for the loss of that Stealth bonus. It's not Disengage actions that take penalties while you try to move while hidden; it's the Stealth action that takes the penalty.<br /> <br /> Also, Disengaging costs 2 Initiative, succeed or fail. So, you could get out of the Stealth-boosted Initiative crash, only for your bow to encourage you to put yourself right back into Initiative Crash as you attempt to run away from a swordsman who already put you into Initiative Crash before.<br /> <br /> Has anyone tried using this Artifact? Has this worked out for them?<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so what about the next level, Half Moon, which is where anyone should be when first rolling Join Battle.<br /> <br /> +2 to Awareness rolls. Which you only get <i>after </i>making possibly the most important Awareness roll of the entire fight. Not even necessarily the Join Battle roll itself, but perhaps an Awareness check beforehand to notice an impending ambush against yourself.<br /> <br /> The level of ironic &quot;Fuck You, Player&quot; is <i>beyond words to describe.</i><br /> <br /> Even aside from that, is the bonus actually useful <i>in</i> a fight in progress? If you've just rolled into combat, any ambushing attacker has probably revealed himself with the opening attack. If you've instead fought your way back up through Initiative Crash and base Initiative, you're <i>hopefully </i>coming out of Stealth, and in the wildest of dreams, you're still <i>in</i> stealth. Being concealed, and not yet having a strong advantage, you're probably wanting more to remain concealed than trying to find anyone else who is concealed, especially because the swordsman beating your ass probably doesn't need to try hiding from you.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next level is Waxing Moon, which offers an even better bonus to disengaging, and an equal one to rushing.<br /> <br /> Why does an archer want to rush anyone? Also, rushing is impossible in stealth without magic, and the bow offers no magic to handle that restriction.<br /> <br /> Also also, why did Disengaging stop being important between the Waning Moon and Waxing Moon stages? Why was Awareness more important in the Half Moon stage?<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, the Full Moon stage lets you reflexive Aim in order to attack targets at long range.<br /> <br /> Wait, is this bow trying to help you achieve safety through range, or stealth? If it was that concerned with range, why the Awareness check half-way through, and why does it give you a Stealth bonus in Crash instead of something more useful for running away, like discounting the Initiative cost of the Disengage action?<br /> <br /> Also, why would the Waxing Moon stage give you the option to rush an opponent when the Full Moon stage encourages you to attack from as far away as possible?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Obviously, this thing is the rushed and poorly considered afterthought of the Corebook, as I've said before. Everything about it is a joke, especially its single boring Evocation, and I can't imagine why the Lunar thought it was worth hiding from the Wyld Hunt. Except maybe to conceal her shame.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, so what ideas <i>can</i> be salvaged from this?<br /> <br /> The basic idea of a bow that grows from concealing darkness to shining strength is workable; make the bow's string a thing of moonlight that disappears when you're Crashed, forcing you to hide without the option of shooting arrows to wither back some Initiative. After you reset, the stealth bonus ends because the string of light has reappeared and you can start making withering attacks again, and the string is brightest and tightest when you have the most Initiative to use for a Decisive shot.<br /> <br /> The attunement bonus' essential idea would make an excellent Artifact cloak. Something that helps conceal you when you're Crashed, but which makes you extremely intimidating when you've got plenty of Initiative for making a lethal Decisive attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-28-2017, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T18:01:19-08:00","id":1163418,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I looked at the leaked copies of the Corebook back when it was under production. I'm sorry, I'm weak.<br /> <br /> I knew very early on that there wasn't going to be a moonsilver artifact in the Core, <i>and I was fine with that.</i><br /> <br /> Sure, I was disappointed, but I wasn't upset. I know there's only so much space in a Corebook, and that coming up with good ideas for Lunars and their metal has proven difficult in the past. Lunars weren't even coming out until after the Exigents, so there was plenty of time for good Lunar/moonsilver stuff later.<br /> <br /> <i>Moonlit Huntress</i> upsets me. Because someone thought that shoving a poorly developed afterthought into the book at the metaphorical last minute was acceptable, when that effort and word-count could have been spent polishing content which was actually worthwhile. Or fixing the disappointing paragraph on the potential of moonsilver.<br /> <br /> This isn't even a recent sentiment, on my part. I'm more disappointed now than before, but it was always obvious how poorly Moonlit Huntress compared to the others. I always knew it was newer than them, as well as shorter, and more boring.<br /> <br /> Sure, it took until now to see just how broken this poor thing is (though anyone who tried to use it out of the box would have figured it out then rather than later), but did no one think we would NOTICE right away that it was pretty poor compared to the other 3-dot Artifacts? Did they think we wouldn't care if the token moonsilver thing was halfhearted, as long as a token of any sort was included?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-28-2017, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T18:08:37-08:00","id":1163420,"title":"","content":"Moonlit Huntress doesn't really work, no. <br /> <br /> At least The Walking Devil Tower is a thing now. And Flying Silver Dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T18:15:43-08:00","id":1163422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163420#post1163420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moonlit Huntress doesn't really work, no.<br /> <br /> At least The Walking Devil Tower is a thing now. And Flying Silver Dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I love <i>Arms of the Chosen</i>.<br /> <br /> Even the stuff that isn't to my taste is really cool, and thoughtfully designed. There's clear inspiration and investment put into the moonsilver and Lunar-made artifacts of <i>Arms</i>, as well as everything else. Even the Lunar hearthstones are awesome, rather than sucking.<br /> <br /> (Seriously, what Exalt would use a greater Lunar demesne, rare as those must be, to build a greater Lunar manse that specifically generates a Beast Gem? Why would <i>players </i>want a Beast Gem? Players don't want to wait an in-game year for a <i>daiklave</i>, let alone a herd of slightly-better mundane cattle!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T19:10:46-08:00","id":1163434,"title":"","content":"The Beast Gem doesn't have any keywords, so it can just form naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T21:09:38-08:00","id":1163465,"title":"","content":"The Beast Gem is extremely valuable to anyone who wants to just settle and develop a region for a while without getting into many fights. It's not something a typical player would be hugely interested in, but it can easily serve a storytelling purpose - a local settlement that has a gem like that can benefit from it a lot, and it could become the macguffin for many stories as a result. (And the fact that people want it could lead players to eg. steal it and give / trade it to someone else.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T21:21:29-08:00","id":1163468,"title":"","content":"Hopefully we\u2019ll eventually get the blog post with all the Corebook Artifacts updates to work with the Resonance/Dissonance System, and Moonlit Huntress can be tweaked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T23:44:36-08:00","id":1163491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163422#post1163422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, what Exalt would use a greater Lunar demesne, rare as those must be, to build a greater Lunar manse that specifically generates a Beast Gem?</div> </div> </div> </div>The kind who wants to breed an army of smart, obedient tyrant lizards, <i>duh</i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T02:17:31-08:00","id":1163503,"title":"","content":"Peaceful farming community grows up around Beast Gem. Players steal it to power Warstrider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T06:06:00-08:00","id":1163523,"title":"","content":"Looking at the beast gem, holy shit this is amazing from an infrastructural perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T07:27:29-08:00","id":1163537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163523#post1163523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at the beast gem, holy shit this is amazing from an infrastructural perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>No question there. But here are two questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Does breeding cattle seem more Luna, Goddess of the Hunt, or Sextes Jylis, Wood Dragon of all forms of organic life?<br /> <br /> 2) Couldn\u2019t this effect be achieved through the manse itself, which could instead make a hearthstone that benefits the traveling Exalted owner?<br /> <br /> Related to (2), wouldn\u2019t a sorcerous working on the land be cheaper?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T07:35:55-08:00","id":1163542,"title":"","content":"If you made the effect with a manse, you'd have to have your manse on a farm. What solar or lunar is going to put their manse on a farm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T07:40:10-08:00","id":1163546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163542#post1163542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you made the effect with a manse, you'd have to have your manse on a farm. What solar or lunar is going to put their manse on a farm?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same Exalt who built a manse that helps with farming? A manse doesn\u2019t have to be larger than a barn, and manses have affected surrounding territories as large as the farmland surrounding a barn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T08:19:02-08:00","id":1163558,"title":"","content":"Yeah, ok, but lunar demesnes are rare. Maybe it's hard to find one in a good place for agriculture. <br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, I'll just keep some cows on this mountain, that'll work.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's like with the Orb of Cool Breezes. Where's that useful? The south. Where are there probably not many air-aspect demesnes you could use to generate the effect with a manse? The south.<br /> <br /> Manses have issues of geography and environment that hearthstones circumvent, and you can't just ignore that when you criticise them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T08:29:14-08:00","id":1163562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163537#post1163537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sextes Jylis, Wood Dragon of all forms of organic life?</div> </div> </div> </div>I might be wrong here... but I think the Wood Element in the Exalted cosmology only covers plants. I don't remembering it even covering things like fungi in past editions (I know mushrooms are an entirely different Kingdom, but they are also sesile organisms, which early cultures might not have always destinguished from plants). <br /> <br /> Also, there are no mentions of Wood Animas sprouting bones, fur, exoskeletons, or any other animal derived growth, starngely not even algae (which again I know are not plants, but see my point about how primitive cultures might have considered them plants above). <br /> <br /> So, I don't know, but it seems to me that in order to &quot;qualify&quot; as an element it is required to... I guess not have a nervous system. Maybe a topic for another conversation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T09:15:30-08:00","id":1163574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163558#post1163558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, ok, but lunar demesnes are rare. Maybe it's hard to find one in a good place for agriculture. <br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, I'll just keep some cows on this mountain, that'll work.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's like with the Orb of Cool Breezes. Where's that useful? The south. Where are there probably not many air-aspect demesnes you could use to generate the effect with a manse? The south.<br /> <br /> Manses have issues of geography and environment that hearthstones circumvent, and you can't just ignore that when you criticise them.</div> </div> </div> </div>By your argument that cold environments produce cold gems, then fertile gems would be produced by fertile environments.<br /> <br /> So if a Lunar manse can produce a fertile breeding gem, then Lunar demesnes are fertile breeding grounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T09:30:39-08:00","id":1163575,"title":"","content":"Given that no one else has had anything to say about Moonlit Huntress, I take it that everyone agrees, and just doesn\u2019t care enough to Like the post to show it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T09:54:19-08:00","id":1163592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163537#post1163537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No question there. But here are two questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Does breeding cattle seem more Luna, Goddess of the Hunt, or Sextes Jylis, Wood Dragon of all forms of organic life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Arms specifically says that there is some overlap in hearthstone types (and IIRC 2e had some gems that could appear from multiple sources.) I wouldn't be surprised if there was also a Wood version of the Beast Gem, or a gem that had a similar effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Couldn\u2019t this effect be achieved through the manse itself, which could instead make a hearthstone that benefits the traveling Exalted owner? </div> </div> </div>The owner might not be a traveling exalt; they could be a god, spirit, mortal sorcerer, or the like. Or it could even occur naturally, with some lucky villagers finding it and hiding it in their village to enjoy its benefits.<br /> <br /> Additionally, there are advantages to having it be portable. Say I'm a local lord. With this hearthstone, I can send it around my lands from season to season to reward favored followers or to improve livestock wherever I feel it's specifically needed. If a famine or other disaster strikes one part of my land, I can quickly send the hearthstone there to help them recover. I can't do that with a manse. I can also loan or trade it out in exchange for favors - suppose I have a good place to build a manse, but what I <i>really</i> need is to win recognition from some local power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Related to (2), wouldn\u2019t a sorcerous working on the land be cheaper? </div> </div> </div>I <i>believe</i> that even mortals can construct manses. They would probably need to bargain for help and support from magical beings (such as spirits), and maybe need someone with heavy-duty occult talent to do some planning and design, but the effort, expenditure, and risk by those people is less than it would take to perform a working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-29-2017, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T10:04:41-08:00","id":1163596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163542#post1163542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you made the effect with a manse, you'd have to have your manse on a farm. What solar or lunar is going to put their manse on a farm?</div> </div> </div> </div>I never before considered <i>Green Acres</i> in the context of Exalted, but now I'm imagining Eva Gabor as a cosmopolitan Eclipse less than thrilled by her Lunar husband's lifestyle choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T11:32:44-08:00","id":1163629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163537#post1163537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No question there. But here are two questions:<br /> <br /> 1) Does breeding cattle seem more Luna, Goddess of the Hunt, or Sextes Jylis, Wood Dragon of all forms of organic life?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it as either. It is kinda on the edge of the moon's themes, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T04:00:27-08:00","id":1163856,"title":"","content":"So I'm a little late here, but I thought I'd post anyway, since I'm running an Exalted 3e game in which our Stealth-supernal Night caste Solar is running around with a beefed up version* of the Moonlit Huntress.<br /> To answer the question posed by the thread subject of &quot;Does it work?&quot;<br /> Oh yes. It works amazingly well as a sniper's bow. If one is using Blinding Battle Feint, the 0 or less effect from the attunement suite serves well, since that auto-success on Stealth is one more point of Init. Couple that with the option to add 15 Initiative with the Evocation - and also reflexively aim as a bonus of the sole published Evocation's interaction with attunement suite - and it allows a stealth archer to drop a rather massive decisive attack on a major threat to open a combat. Probably from Ambush or at least Surprise.<br /> Now, is that good for the intended dramatic combat flow? I would say, no. While my player has certainly felt amazingly bad-ass, it did cut short a battle involving a noteworthy Sidereal adversary when said Night shot him through the organ(s) of her choosing as her opening action of the combat. (Incapacitated - and then some!)<br /> Is the Moonlit Huntress designed well in keeping with a theme?<br /> Honestly, there's simply too little there to judge. But if you postulate that Lunars will have a Charm to substitute Stealth for the usual Join Battle roll - and I hope that they will, given that 'Sneaky Predator' is one of the themes they should be expected to carry - I don't think the low end attunement effect is all that bad. I do agree that the overall array of effects is a mish-mash of confusion. The attunement suite seems inspired by the phases of the moon more than by the story of the Huntress itself. If I had it all to do over, I might revamp the effects for my player at my table such that they're more generally useful or at least more fitting.<br /> <br /> Somewhat off-topic: Regarding the &quot;beefed up version&quot; the player in question wanted to put a full 5 dots into the Moonlit Huntress with the understanding that it would receive a commensurate upgrade to the number Evocations it would have. We agreed to keep all the basics intact - largely because this is our first 3e game and no one wanted to hold it up on me workshopping even more artifacts. I added a few Evocations later - and modified the backstory a bit. I can get into that elsewhere, but suffice to say, it's still a WIP and I'm still trying to marry some good mechanics to its theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11647-gargoyle","name":"Gargoyle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T04:18:38-08:00","id":1163858,"title":"","content":"Not sure you needed to increase the cost for extra evocations. It still has 8 or 9 free slots as written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T05:42:55-08:00","id":1163877,"title":"","content":"And I think being able to buy a heap of Initiative just by paying a point of Willpower is broken and boring.<br /> <br /> There are Solar Charms that give you drips or small chunks of Initiative as a reward for <i>doing things.</i> The larger chunks require you to roll Join Battle to determine how large, and only after you have done something interesting and relevant.<br /> <br /> None of them are as amazing or easy as this stupid Evocation.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I do really appreciate you posting your personal experience with the weapon. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 11-30-2017, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T05:56:01-08:00","id":1163880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163629#post1163629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could see it as either. It is kinda on the edge of the moon's themes, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you say it was on the edge of Wood\u2019s themes? Or instead, at least a little closer to the center?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T06:05:43-08:00","id":1163883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163880#post1163880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you say it was on the edge of Wood\u2019s themes? Or instead, at least a little closer to the center?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since it's dealing with Fauna instead of flora, it's further from the center of Wood's Themes than it could be. Probably a little bit closer to the center of Wood's Themes than the Moon's themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:43:01-08:00","id":1163915,"title":"","content":"Animal life is in Wood elements periphery. It works on vitality and stuff, either promoting it or attacking it with poisons.<br /> <br /> But the beast gem isn't just about making animals healthy. It makes them smarter and stronger too, as well as easier to tame. Those are more Lunar themes that Wood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:47:08-08:00","id":1163916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163915#post1163915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animal life is in Wood elements periphery. It works on vitality and stuff, either promoting it or attacking it with poisons.<br /> <br /> But the beast gem isn't just about making animals healthy. It makes them smarter and stronger too, as well as easier to tame. Those are more Lunar themes that Wood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wood Abilities include Ride and Survival for taming, empowering, and breeding animals. Also Medicine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:53:57-08:00","id":1163920,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but the point is that it's more Lunar (and Wood) than Wood (and Lunar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T09:32:37-08:00","id":1163956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163537#post1163537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Does breeding cattle seem more Luna, Goddess of the Hunt, or Sextes Jylis, Wood Dragon of all forms of organic life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Source material is helpful here. Artemis/Diana, often associated with the moon, was a goddess of the hunt, the wilderness, wild animals, birth, the young of all species, and girl children before marriage.<br /> <br /> So it isn't really about breeding, its about strong young. Now as for why it is only trained animals, your guess is as good as mine, though I suspect gamist reasons to avoid making it even more unattractive from making all the local wolves smarter or having to think about the impact of all the animals being super intelligent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T19:37:27-08:00","id":1164153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1163956#post1163956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now as for why it is only trained animals, your guess is as good as mine, though I suspect gamist reasons to avoid making it even more unattractive from making all the local <b>wolves</b> smarter or having to think about the impact of all the animals being super intelligent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or river dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T10:46:56-07:00","id":1227699,"title":"","content":"Okay, so this discussion is not over, because some people think this bow is good.<br /> <br /> Well, kindly read the first post and make a case.<br /> <br /> <br /> Keep in mind that \u201cgood\u201d and \u201cpowerful\u201d are two different things. First Edition\u2019s Deadly Beastman Transformsation was one of the most powerful Charms in the game... and also one of the worst-designed. Likewise, Blade of the Battle-Maiden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-15-2018, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T11:45:13-07:00","id":1227708,"title":"","content":"I am very fond of its attunement bonus and would love to give it a real Evocation tree that expressed Luna's aspects/Other Moons through the lens of a longbow.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T12:21:50-07:00","id":1227715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1227708#post1227708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very fond of its attunement bonus and would love to give it a real Evocation tree that expressed Luna's aspects/Other Moons through the lens of a longbow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the attunement bonus would also need fixing.<br /> <br /> It could give you a withering attack bonus when you\u2019re crashed, discount the Initiative cost of Disengage actions when you are at base initiative or lower, and definitely should never give you a Rush bonus.<br /> <br /> Bows are most accurate at short range and least accurate at close range. A Lunar at close range can maul someone in the form of a bear or tyrant lizard. This bow shouldn\u2019t help you rush!<br /> <br /> Especially not when the phase beyond that one rewards you for being at long range!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T12:58:49-07:00","id":1227731,"title":"","content":"I would rather compliment them with charms that encouraged that particular course of action than replace them with more generic bonuses. For example, the idea of the Exalt being initiative crashed and <i>disappearing</i> is evocative and not at all in line with my expectations of what someone would do in that situation in 3e combat.<br /> <br /> That said I don't know what to do with Half Moon so I am not married to this. But I can absolutely have fun with the other four.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T13:29:47-07:00","id":1227737,"title":"","content":"The Half Moon bonus is objectively the worst, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T16:36:28-07:00","id":1227783,"title":"","content":"So, what even is Moonlit Huntress' theme or story? The introduction blurb hints at &quot;hunting&quot;, but the attunement bonus is less about stalking or sniping and more about combat in general.<br /> <br /> The single Evocation is likewise about combat in general, but isn't unlocked by significant battles or hunts. In fact, the &quot;special condition&quot; doesn't even unlock the Evocation for free; after being made to wait arbitrarily for two stories regardless of what sort of stories they are or what you do, you still have to pay for this broken Evocation.<br /> <br /> Ugh, I hate how boring it is. Even the name is uninspired. It's just the weapon's name with the word Aura slapped on the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T14:07:45-07:00","id":1227897,"title":"","content":"My basic notion of evocations that synergise with the blessings.<br /> <br /> No Moon- Works with the idea of making an unexpected attack to turn the tide of the combat, this is something the system does not generally do and unexpected attacks are usually decisive attacks made from a position of strength.<br /> <br /> Waning Moon- Facilitates some level of disengagement shooting, probably make it withering-only both to have synergy with the blessing and to prevent a boring wielder from walking backwards and shooting arrows until their opponent dies.<br /> <br /> Half Moon- Not a clue!<br /> <br /> Waxing Moon- Encourages getting in close because its not what anyone would expect you to do with a bow. Thinking it maybe has some kind of relationship to cover and heavily armoured foes like climbing a warstrider to shoot the vision slits.<br /> <br /> Full Moon- Something sniping related? Its using the bow at optimal range and with optimal initiative so it needs to not be too generic. <br /> <br /> Moonlit Huntress Aura- Remade loosely based on Superior Violent Knowledge allowing you to bank x points of Initiative to summon back later in the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-16T14:47:47-07:00","id":1227903,"title":"","content":"Hmm, developing a full version of it... I wonder if there could be some kind of across the board system based on shifting through a cycle, similar to other ones with unique fuel sources or similar quirks. Possibly make the one Evocation with five phases into a starting power and then... something else for when it shifts between them.<br /> <br /> Or maybe break the five-phase power up and distribute it around, with accessibility based on the cycle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T12:06:45-07:00","id":1228084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1227897#post1227897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My basic notion of evocations that synergise with the blessings.<br /> <br /> No Moon- Works with the idea of making an unexpected attack to turn the tide of the combat, this is something the system does not generally do and unexpected attacks are usually decisive attacks made from a position of strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before that, the bow would need to do more to help you actually become concealed. <br /> <br /> You seldom get to choose where you are when someone crashes you, and you could find yourself without sufficient cover to justify an attempt at concealment. Especially if the opponent that crashed you is at close range. <br /> <br /> As a three-dot Artifact, Moonlit Huntress has the least possible number of Evocations to unlock. Do you really want to spend two or three of them on \u201chiding while crashed\u201d as opposed to Evocations that could help you avoid being crashed in the first place?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Waning Moon- Facilitates some level of disengagement shooting, probably make it withering-only both to have synergy with the blessing and to prevent a boring wielder from walking backwards and shooting arrows until their opponent dies. </div> </div> </div>Solar Archery has Hunter\u2019s Swift Answer. Terrestrial Archery doesn\u2019t because Terrestrials are bad at generating reflexive, additional actions; a weakness likely not shared by other Celestial Exalted. <br /> <br /> Also, Disengaging is designed to not be boring, given the tension between it and Rushing. Disengaging and shooting would also normally require flurries, which makes both actions more likely to fail. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Waxing Moon- Encourages getting in close because its not what anyone would expect you to do with a bow. </div> </div> </div>For good reason: It\u2019s a terrible idea, and one that works against everything else the bow is doing. Stealth, Disengaging, aiming reflexively from long range... everything else about the bow is playing to the strength of the bow, which is avoiding fights at close-range. <br /> <br /> And like I said, the next phase after that one is completely pointless if you\u2019re not at long range. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Moonlit Huntress Aura- Remade loosely based on Superior Violent Knowledge allowing you to bank x points of Initiative to summon back later in the scene. </div> </div> </div>So you can either use it to conserve some Initiative you\u2019re sure you don\u2019t need to blow on a decisive attack, or use it to make a decisive attack while crashed.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not a big fan of that Brawl Charm, but I agree it is a much better Charm than Moonlit Huntress Aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T13:11:38-07:00","id":1228099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1228084#post1228084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before that, the bow would need to do more to help you actually become concealed.<br /> <br /> You seldom get to choose where you are when someone crashes you, and you could find yourself without sufficient cover to justify an attempt at concealment. Especially if the opponent that crashed you is at close range.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think where we disagree on this is that I see no problem with a charm that expects you to develop a particular skillset in order to make full use of it. Its like Rumour of Form is an overpriced version of Hail Shattering Practice if you insist on using it the same way and refuse to invest in Stealth and let the reflexive action it creates go to waste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you really want to spend two or three of them on \u201chiding while crashed\u201d as opposed to Evocations that could help you avoid being crashed in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think surprise withering attacks are an interesting place to go as they are not normally encouraged by the combat system and not something you would only do while crashed. Ever seen movies where the protagonists are menaced by an unseen shooter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Disengaging is designed to not be boring, given the tension between it and Rushing. Disengaging and shooting would also normally require flurries, which makes both actions more likely to fail.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, but we are talking about an artifact that can greatly enhance disengage attempts. My reasoning with it being withering-only was that it could push someone wielding it out of the Waning Moon blessing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And like I said, the next phase after that one is completely pointless if you\u2019re not at long range.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do not necessarily see the problem with that. The way I see it Moonlit Huntress has 5 attunement bonuses if there is a logical progression from No Moon &gt; Waning Moon &gt; Half Moon &gt; Waxing Moon &gt; Full Moon then it would be overpowered as hell. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So you can either use it to conserve some Initiative you\u2019re sure you don\u2019t need to blow on a decisive attack, or use it to make a decisive attack while crashed.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not a big fan of that Brawl Charm, but I agree it is a much better Charm than Moonlit Huntress Aura.</div> </div> </div> </div> I appreciate tactical banking of initiative, less so the whole mess about making decisive attacks in initiative crash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T14:28:46-07:00","id":1228116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1228099#post1228099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think where we disagree on this is that I see no problem with a charm that expects you to develop a particular skillset in order to make full use of it. Its like Rumour of Form is an overpriced version of Hail Shattering Practice if you insist on using it the same way and refuse to invest in Stealth and let the reflexive action it creates go to waste.</div> </div> </div> </div>But we're talking about an attunement bonus and ground-level Charm. That's equivalent to the pre-form Charms of a Martial Arts Style, which are not designed to be nearly useless without a bunch of Charms from a completely different Ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think surprise withering attacks are an interesting place to go as they are not normally encouraged by the combat system and not something you would only do while crashed. Ever seen movies where the protagonists are menaced by an unseen shooter? </div> </div> </div>The difference is that unseen shooters can remain unseen without magic, whereas in Exalted, you break concealment completely by making any attack, and need to succeed at a concealment action to disappear again. The point of making surprise or ambush decisive attacks is making sure there's no one alive to care.<br /> <br /> But trying to make nothing but surprise withering attacks at close or short range is crazy, especially against an opponent dangerous enough to crash you. At long range, you have enough space to hide before they catch up with you, but at close range, you have nothing to buy that time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but we are talking about an artifact that can greatly enhance disengage attempts. </div> </div> </div>+2 dice to Disengage at the cost of immediately going into crash (or doing so with the very next attempt) doesn't sound all that &quot;great&quot; to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do not necessarily see the problem with that. The way I see it Moonlit Huntress has 5 attunement bonuses if there is a logical progression from No Moon &gt; Waning Moon &gt; Half Moon &gt; Waxing Moon &gt; Full Moon then it would be overpowered as hell. </div> </div> </div>Leaving that aside, there's nothing about this weapon that makes a bonus to Rushing a good idea, and it's contrary to everything else the weapon is doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T15:03:30-07:00","id":1228125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1228116#post1228116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we're talking about an attunement bonus and ground-level Charm. That's equivalent to the pre-form Charms of a Martial Arts Style, which are not designed to be nearly useless without a bunch of Charms from a completely different Ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of Martial Arts charms enhance Rush and Disengage actions, their value without investment in Athletics or Dodge is pretty questionable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But trying to make nothing but surprise withering attacks at close or short range is crazy, especially against an opponent dangerous enough to crash you. At long range, you have enough space to hide before they catch up with you, but at close range, you have nothing to buy that time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about the charm having functionality beyond its synergy with the No Moon Blessing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">+2 dice to Disengage at the cost of immediately going into crash (or doing so with the very next attempt) doesn't sound all that &quot;great&quot; to me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Unless you hit your opponent with your attack at which point you gain initiative or reset.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T15:08:56-07:00","id":1228126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1228116#post1228116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving that aside, there's nothing about this weapon that makes a bonus to Rushing a good idea, and it's contrary to everything else the weapon is doing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There actually is - it's the fact that it's a moonsilver weapon, implying that it was made for a Lunar.<br /> <br /> Rushing into melee after building up some initiative by shooting may be a terrible idea for an ability exalt whose powerset encourages them to push increasingly further into crippling overspecialization territory, but given that Lunars are hardly incentivized to pick one method of combat over another (no favored ability bonuses and ability-independent excellencies mean that you're actually better off maintaining a suite of two or three combat abilities at 3 each instead of going for 5 in one and neglecting the rest), rushing in to finish a character off might actually make perfect sense.<br /> <br /> I think there is definitely a design space for moonsilver weapons that encourage behavior which seems somewhere between strange and counterproductive to characters that are more limited in the number of ways they can approach a situation than Luna's Chosen are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-17T15:33:39-07:00","id":1228134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bastet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1228125#post1228125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of Martial Arts charms enhance Rush and Disengage actions, their value without investment in Athletics or Dodge is pretty questionable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Charms work even when you're not crashed, though. Also, you can generally Rush and Disengage without assistance in most situations, whereas you cannot attempt concealment without cover or the ability to ignore the need for cover.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was talking about the charm having functionality beyond its synergy with the No Moon Blessing. </div> </div> </div>You mean that you think Moonlit Huntress should have an Evocation that enhances attempts to hide even when you're not crashed?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless you hit your opponent with your attack at which point you gain initiative or reset. </div> </div> </div>As I said, attempting to disengage and attack at the same time makes both actions more prone to failure, and Disengaging costs you initiative even if you fail.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1228126#post1228126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There actually is - it's the fact that it's a moonsilver weapon, implying that it was made for a Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would be wrong. It was made by a Lunar, for a Solar.<br /> <br /> I'm also highly doubtful that its appropriate for Evocations to enhance actions that do not involve using the artifact in question. Even for moonsilver.<br /> <br /> I don't want to see anyone try to characterize moonsilver as the &quot;lol, random&quot; metal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T01:36:28-07:00","id":1228229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1228134#post1228134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also highly doubtful that its appropriate for Evocations to enhance actions that do not involve using the artifact in question. Even for moonsilver.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> - Frost-Thorn Knuckles allows you to increase your soak when unarmored, ignore environmental hazards and waive the cost of a Survival Charm<br /> - Summer Thunder can <i>increase your mount's Speed bonus</i> (totally something that involves using your artifact, right?) and waive the initiative cost of disengaging while inflicting an initiative penalty on opposing enemies<br /> - Sun's Brush allows you to reflexively introduce facts (that's something you can use a grimcleaver for?)<br /> - Talion enhances read intentions actions (also the kind of thing where having a weapon usually helps)<br /> - Gorgon can turn disengage successes into failures (although you could argue that it is the imprisoned demon's lethargy leaking out, so while not <i>technically </i>an action that uses the artifact, it could be interpreted as one in spirit)<br /> - Baldaquin enhances Resolve and Guile in the courts of spirits and the Fair Folk, makes a handful of Sail, Presence and Bureaucracy Charms more effective, gives rerolls on bargain and read intentions actions while acting as an intermediary, and bestows the Eclipse diplomatic immunity on other envoys as spelled out in the terms of an agreement - none of these involve donning an armor<br /> - Kaijin adds bonus successes to Manipulation-based influence rolls while speaking Old Realm<br /> - ...actually most of the armors do things that have nothing to do with using them, so I won't list every single example<br /> <br /> <br /> Based on this fairly cursory reading of Arms, I think we can safely say that it is perfectly appropriate for an Evocation to enhance <i>whatever action you want</i> as long as it fits the artifact's unique legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T02:09:22-07:00","id":1228232,"title":"","content":"Artifacts you wear lend themselves more easily to passive effects like that. A weapon should probably restrict itself to stuff you would naturally do while holding it. <br /> <br /> It'd be weird if you go to a gala and try to seduce someone while waving about a goremaul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T02:39:49-07:00","id":1228238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1228232#post1228232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts you wear lend themselves more easily to passive effects like that. A weapon should probably restrict itself to stuff you would naturally do while holding it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're welcome to tell the designers of Frost-Thorn Knuckles, Sun's Brush, Summer Thunder and Talion that they made their artifacts wrong, I guess?<br /> <br /> Edit: this may have come off as more hostile than I intended. However, I think that the primary goal of artifact design should be to produce something that results in a fun play experience, not to uphold some abstract design principle like &quot;a weapon's Evocations must fit these specific criteria otherwise it's Bad&quot;. As long as the end result is coherent, anything should be fair game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 06-18-2018, 05:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T02:53:45-07:00","id":1228240,"title":"","content":"You wear frost-thorn knuckles. They're basically gloves.<br /> <br /> As for the other three, Sun's brush largely facilitates introducing facts <i>in combat</i> to aid said combat. Summer Thunder is all about mounted combat, where you would naturally be carrying a bow. Talion is a staff. You can carry those anywhere. And it still mostly helps in combat. <br /> <br /> So no, I wouldn't say they made their artifacts wrong. They all fulfil my criterion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-18-2018, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T03:27:08-07:00","id":1228243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1228240#post1228240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You wear frost-thorn knuckles. They're basically gloves.<br /> <br /> As for the other three, Sun's brush largely facilitates introducing facts <i>in combat</i> to aid said combat. Summer Thunder is all about mounted combat, where you would naturally be carrying a bow. Talion is a staff. You can carry those anywhere. And it still mostly helps in combat.<br /> <br /> So no, I wouldn't say they made their artifacts wrong. They all fulfil my criterion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm genuinely having trouble trying to suss out the reasoning behind &quot;improving your mount's abilities with a bow or your read intentions actions with a staff is A-OK but a bow that helps you rush people is bad design&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T03:31:59-07:00","id":1228245,"title":"","content":"Oh, there's nothing wrong with that. I was just saying that &quot;whatever action you want&quot; was perhaps a bit too large a generalisation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T05:11:06-07:00","id":1228256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1163401-does-moonlit-huntress-work?p=1228243#post1228243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm genuinely having trouble trying to suss out the reasoning behind &quot;improving your mount's abilities with a bow or your read intentions actions with a staff is A-OK but a bow that helps you rush people is bad design&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> right, we think it is perfectly fine for a bow to enhance a Rush action, but only if the bow is specialized to function best in close range.<br /> <br /> Moonlit Huntress is not that bow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T05:29:22-07:00","id":1228259,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I forget where I posted it, but I tried to figure out a fix for this bow once and one of the things I did was make the full moon power the no moon power, because I figured that made more sense as a long range ability a sniper might use, and follows from waning's disengage bonus. The full moon ability should facilitate close range combat because it follows from waxing moon granting a bonus to rush, and works as a &quot;get up in opponent's face&quot; tactic. <br /> <br /> I just had the half-moon power be on by default because then it's actually useful for join battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T16:38:36-07:00","id":1228410,"title":"","content":"I wonder as I look at Moonlit Huntress if it's not making a statement on Lunar Flexibility by it's lack of existence. Maybe, in some way, the lack of focus on the bow; it's limited charms but spread attunement bonuses, is suggesting the flexibility that Lunars and Moonsilver both share. Maybe the idea for the weapon is that if you take it, you'll pick which of the attunement bonuses you like best, and start making evocations to give you bonuses like that; a sniper, a sneaky stealth archer, a distance closing chaser, etc. In that way you can customize the weapon more effecitvely for the kind of fighter you are, using Moonsilver's flexibility as a jumping off point.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's a legitimate question here of 'is this a good design space when you give someone a mostly blank weapon, don't explain anything and expect them to connect the dots?' and honestly it's really not. Not in the core book at least; Wise Steel and Razor Dancer does something similar but it's in the Evocation book specifically, which is probably a much better place to have something like this, where you can devote wordcount to such an idea, and give a better Moonsilver weapon in the core.<br /> <br /> It's not good, but it's something I could understand being the idea behind, though I may also be giving too much credit to those two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T18:25:09-07:00","id":1228437,"title":"","content":"Wise Steel and Razor Dancer at least have the excuse of being freshly made; too young to have many Evocations yet discovered.<br /> <br /> Moonlit Huntress is explicitly at least a few centuries older than the Usurpation, and used frequently by at least two Exalted before being used by a third.<br /> <br /> The simple answer is that the attunement bonus has so much wordcount to it precisely because the author must have been trying to make the weapon seem as impressive as possible with only that and a single, overpowered Evocation.<br /> <br /> Once again, I state my opinion that I would have been less insulted if no one had even bothered to try writing this thing at the last minute; if someone had just acknowledged that they didn't have any moonsilver artifact worth the wordcount ready for the corebook.<br /> <br /> <br /> Normally, an artifact like Moonlit Huntress would have had at least five Evocations, one for each lunar phase, rather than cramming all of the phases into the attunement bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-18-2018, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T19:42:59-07:00","id":1228465,"title":"","content":"I'm not really going to defend the artifact as it is, because it was made by someone who isn't me and I don't know their thought process, I was just offering a suggestion.<br /> <br /> But what I can say is, as politely as possible, ask you to please be less rude. Not to me, really, or whatever; you're civil enough. But to people who wrote this stuff. This game is supposed to be inclusive, and the forums are supposed to be welcoming. In theory, the person who wrote Moonlit Huntress is a fan of Exalted, has played it, and probably is at least a member of these forums. But this thread, whenever you bring it back up and you go through it, you realize it's literally just you, sometimes against a person, sometimes just posting with yourself, about how bad this specific artifact and how insulted you are, personally, by the fact it exists. You do repeatedly use the word 'insulted', that's your main crux; that you're insulted that this exists and it offends you. If I was a writer, especially if I had wrote this, I'm not sure I'd ever want to write for this game again, if my best effort had been responded to by a forums poster literally making a topic about how awful it was.<br /> <br /> We don't know the situation of the artifact, the word count, any of that. We don't know who wrote it, or why they wrote it. We just know what's in the book. And you don't like it. That's fine! I don't like shit in the books either! But making threads about parts I super hate feels like it could just hurt someone's feelings, and in some way that feels counterproductive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-18T21:11:04-07:00","id":1228492,"title":"","content":"I am ashamed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}